<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mitridate, re di Ponto</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1770">1770</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mitridate, re di Ponto is an opera seria in three acts by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wolfgang-amadeus-mozart">Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart</a>, written when he was fourteen and first performed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a> on 26 December 1770. The libretto by Vittorio Amedeo Cigna-Santi is based on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jean-racine">Racine</a>'s tragedy Mithridate. It tells of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mithridates-vi-of-pontus">Mithridates VI of Pontus</a> and his two sons' rivalry for his betrothed, Aspasia, and was Mozart's first great success in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mitridate-re-di-ponto.jpg" alt="Mitridate, re di Ponto" width="320" height="396" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: anonymous · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_of_Wolfgang_Amadeus_Mozart_at_the_age_of_13_in_Verona,_1770.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
